{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/991276-keeping-aesthetics-distinct","id":991276,"title":"Keeping aesthetics distinct","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-21T22:04:41-07:00","id":991276,"title":"Keeping aesthetics distinct","content":"Has anyone given any thought to how to keep traits and aesthetics distinct between various types of supernatural phenomena/beings? It's not the kind of thing you need to worry about as much if you're ruling that, say, only Awakening's cosmology exists or only the Wyrd exists, but if you like putting together a crossover setting and actually using crossovers, figuring out how to keep elements from different lines aesthetically and thematically distinct is something I think about a lot. I'm always asking &quot;what is it specifically about this being that makes them fit best as a True Fae, as opposed to an Abyssal or an Idigam&quot;? Of course, there's bound to be some overlap, and you can even deliberately do this to throw the players for a loop. And supernatural phenomena seem to be subject to convergent evolution and even sometimes deliberately mimic other beings (I've always loved the idea of some occultist trying to do a supernatural ecology).<br /> <br /> As an example, I wouldn't have an angel or demon look too human in their true form. I could see them as having a beautiful true form, in the way a statue or a machine or a work of art can be beautiful, but not just a beautiful human. I don't see the Machine as having that much of an understanding of humanity or a regard for them for its associated phenomena to take that shape. For the True Fae, however, it's something I would definitely consider, since they have a much closer relationship to the dreams and stories of humanity than the Machine does. And this in turn brings us to themes and aesthetics. The Machine is scary because it doesn't really care about humanity, but the Gentry are scary because they care too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:16:37-07:00","id":991362,"title":"","content":"Ummm..... not sure what you're asking. By default, they're all already distinct and separate. Pretty much everyone has pre-defined playgrounds with little to no crossover (except the Hisil and the occasional ghost). They all engage in things that have nothing to do with other splats. Every game has its specialties and individual themes and aethetics. If anything, the trouble is finding things they have in common in order to make crossover happen smoothly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T07:12:55-07:00","id":991383,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, while the form you see when encountering a True Fae is humanoid, that isn't their &quot;true form&quot;. They don't really <i>have</i> a true form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:48:11-07:00","id":991447,"title":"","content":"Not quite sure what the question is.<br /> <br /> Yes, some things overlap. Both Abyssals and idigam want to become something. An Abyssal, however, is something that is impossible for one reason or another but usually because it would work against something that already exists. 'We already have a history,' or 'gravity doesn't work like that,' and so forth. In its fitting in, it corrupts things. An alternate history isn't usually an alternate history of a rock no one's ever seen before, but the entire world, and it must therefore change the entire world to fit it. It spreads. Like a dot of red paint on a white wall, in order to fit in it must repaint the entire wall.<br /> <br /> An idigam actually manages to find a way to fit in with the Fallen World, for instance becoming an underworld or afterlife, or a new kind of spirit, or Father Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:52:21-07:00","id":991450,"title":"","content":"I think I understand what you're saying. For me, the various hunter groups have very distinct styles of how you can describe their merits between them. Like how a high tech TFV safehouse filled with technological safeguards and a Union safehouse outside the city with a shotgun at the door are the same merit, but descriptively unique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T10:54:17-07:00","id":991452,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's also a big part of it. Of course, with Hunter, playing around with the themes and aesthetics of the monsters works especially well as a way to keep the players guessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}